# Who reviews what (GOVERNANCE.md), in the public repository bloque-app/bezent. The teams must exist
# in bloque-app.

*                       @bloque-app/bezent-maintainers

# The specification and its amendments: the spec owner rules on them.
/SPEC.md                @bloque-app/bezent-spec-owner
/amendments/            @bloque-app/bezent-spec-owner
/GOVERNANCE.md          @bloque-app/bezent-spec-owner

# Licensing: the boundary between the GPL parts and the permissive parts.
/docs/oss/              @bloque-app/bezent-spec-owner
/REUSE.toml             @bloque-app/bezent-maintainers
/LICENSES/              @bloque-app/bezent-spec-owner

# The criteria map and the release gate: what V0 must show before it carries value.
/e2e/criteria/          @bloque-app/bezent-spec-owner
/release/               @bloque-app/bezent-spec-owner

# The gate itself: code that decides whether V0 may carry value must not be changeable by the release it judges
# (it runs the tagged commit's own copy). Its CI job is part of the ci.yml file, which the maintainers own; the
# job's name is what branch protection should require (release/README.md, "Settings that make the gate bind").
/tools/ci/              @bloque-app/bezent-spec-owner
/.github/workflows/release-gate.yml  @bloque-app/bezent-spec-owner
